<section id="become">
<div class="container">
<div class="row">
<div class="col-md-12">
<div class="left-banner">
<h3>Are you Interested in Becoming a Participant in the Canadian Depository for Securities (CDS)?</h3>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="teal">
<div class="container">
<div class="row top-row">
<div class="col-12">
<div class="section-header text-center">
<h2>Post Trade Solutions That Meet Your Needs</h2>
</div>
<p>CDS Clearing and Depository Services Inc. (CDS Clearing) is Canada’s Central Securities Depository, Equities clearing and settlement system, and Fixed Income Settlement system. We offer a full suite of securities clearing, settlement, and depository services to domestic and foreign financial services firms, including the following:</p>
<div class="row pt-4">
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="become-card">
<span><img src="/assets/application/img/participant-icon-00.svg" alt="Depository" title="Depository"></span>
<h4>Depository</h4>
<p>CDS Clearing offers a centralized safekeeping facility, allowing securities to be held in a dematerialized form, eliminating the risk related to holding physical financial securities.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="become-card">
<span><img src="/assets/application/img/participant-icon-02.svg" alt="Clearing & Settlement" title="Clearing & Settlement"></span>
<h4>Clearing & Settlement</h4>
<p>CDS Clearing’s post trade services include both a Securities Settlement Service (SSS) and a Central Counterparty (CCP) Service, each of which operates to optimize the efficiency of the clearing and settlement of securities transactions.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="become-card">
<span><img src="/assets/application/img/participant-icon-03.svg" alt="Corporate Action / Entitlement Processing" title="Corporate Action / Entitlement Processing"></span>
<h4>Corporate Action / Entitlement Processing</h4>
<p>In our role as CSD, CDS Clearing provides a centralized source for Canadian Corporate Action Information which enhances timely, accurate, and efficient notification and processing of corporate action events and the payment of entitlements.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="become-card">
<span><img src="/assets/application/img/participant-icon-04.svg" alt="Tax Withholding and Reporting" title="Tax Withholding and Reporting"></span>
<h4>Tax Withholding and Reporting</h4>
<p>CDS Clearing provides tax withholding and tax reporting services on entitlement payments in both Canadian and US Dollars.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="become-card">
<span><img src="/assets/application/img/participant-icon-05.svg" alt="International Link with the US Depository" title="International Link with the US Depository"></span>
<h4>International Link with the US Depository</h4>
<p>Enable seamless cross-border securities transfers and depository services.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="become-card">
<span><img src="/assets/application/img/participant-icon-01.svg" alt="Data Services" title="Data Services"></span>
<h4>Data Services</h4>
<p>CDS Clearing provides the securities and transactional data via Files and real-time messages. Participants can elect to subscribe to additional data services according to their needs.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="teal-grey">
<div class="container">
<div class="row bottom-row">
<div class="col-12">
<div class="section-header text-center">
<h3>Several Participation Types Provide Flexible Solutions for Your Business</h3>
</div>
<div class="row">
<div class="col-md-6">
<div class="white-card">
<h4>Full Participation</h4>
<p>Access a full suite of Post Trade Depository and Clearing Services</p>
<ul>
<li><span class="icon-check"></span>Trade Clearing and Settlement</li>
<li><span class="icon-check"></span>Book Entry Only - Dematerialized Security Positions</li>
<li><span class="icon-check"></span>Corporate Actions Event and Entitlement Payment Processing</li>
<li><span class="icon-check"></span>Tax Reporting</li>
<li><span class="icon-check"></span>Sponsorship into the US Depository (The Depository Trust & Clearing Corporation (DTCC)) for Cross-Border Services </li>
<li><span class="icon-check"></span>Support for Service Providers and 3rd party vendors</li>
<li><span class="icon-check"></span>Access to ISIN Issuance as the National Numbering Agency for Canadian Securities</li>
<li><span class="icon-check"></span>Support for Security Eligibility in CDS</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-6">
<div class="white-card">
<h4>Limited Participation</h4>
<p>If your firm does not require the full suite of CDS Clearing participant Services, CDS Clearing also offers Participation types to match your needs and technological requirements, including:</p>
<div class="border-row">
<h5>Limited Purpose Transfer Agent Participation</h5>
<p>A trust company, bank, or similar institution engaged by a corporation for the purposes of maintaining an Issuer’s books and records and managing an Issuer’s outstanding securities issuances.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-row">
<h5>Depositary Agency</h5>
<p>A Depositary Agent acts as the receiver of securities and instructions when a shareholder must take action on distribution events with options, mandatory exchange events with options or voluntary events.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-row">
<h5>Limited Purpose Account Transfer Online Notifications (ATON) Participation</h5>
<p>Access to CDS Clearing’s ATON Service enables the electronic transfer of client assets and funds between financial intermediaries.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="submit">
<div class="container">
<div class="section-header m-0">
<h2>Getting Started with Your Application for Participation</h2>
</div>
<p class="mt-0 mb-5">We look forward to working with you to identify the appropriate participation type for your organization and guiding your organization through the application process. Below is information that will help you assess your eligibility and provide insight into the application process.</p>
<div class="row">
<div class="col-md-6">
<h3>Check Your Eligibility</h3>
<p>Review the <a href="https://www.cds.ca/resource/en/660" target="_blank">CDS Participant Rules</a>, Rule 2.2 to confirm your eligibility for participation. You will need to assess these requirements against your organization’s needs and technology posture.</p>
<a href="https://www.cds.ca/resource/en/660" class="btn white-button">View Rules</a>
</div>
<div class="col-md-6">
<h3>Review the CDS Financial Risk Model</h3>
<p>The TMX-CDS Financial <a href="https://www.cds.ca/resource/en/56?_ga=2.220697880.1292514237.1741628595-448198197.1727361145" target="_blank">risk model</a> safeguards security transactions in the Depository, settlement and Central counterparty services. It identifies, assesses, and mitigates potential risks to CDS and to Participants, ensuring smooth and secure operations.</p>
<a href="https://www.cds.ca/resource/en/56" class="btn white-button">View Risk Model</a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="phases-new" class="teal-grey">
<div class="container">
<div class="section-header">
<h2>Application Phases</h2>
</div>
<div class="row">
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="phases-card">
<span>1</span>
<h3>Application and Fees</h3>
<p>Our team is happy to meet with you to provide an overview of the application process and the necessary documentation requirements when you are ready.</p>
<a href="https://services.cds.ca/cdsforms/files/CDSX00001.pdf" class="btn secondary-button">Application</a>
<a href="http://services.cds.ca/applications/webforms/onlineforms.nsf/PublishedAll-Web-EN-?&_ga=2.241245954.1297387858.1732565698-445069908.1697214810" class="btn secondary-button">Forms</a>
<a href="https://www.cds.ca/resource/en/275/" class="btn secondary-button">Fees</a>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="phases-card">
<span>2</span>
<h3>Application Submission</h3>
<p>Complete the application form, gather all required documentation, and submit for review, along with the application fee.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="phases-card">
<span>3</span>
<h3>Internal Review & Approval</h3>
<p>We will review the documents to ensure compliance with regulatory requirements and established standards. Upon approval, you will be notified.</p>
<p>Additional Time and approvals are required for foreign clients.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="phases-card">
<span>4</span>
<h3>System Integration / Technical Connectivity</h3>
<p>Set up and connect your systems with TMX-CDS’s platform to prepare for testing. Identify standard file and message subscriptions. TMX-CDS will work with your business and technical contacts as we guide you through this process.</p>
<a href="https://www.cds.ca/resource/en/74" class="btn secondary-button">Technical Guides</a>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="phases-card">
<span>5</span>
<h3>Testing Prior to Moving to Production</h3>
<p>Prior to setting a date to move into production, conduct testing in CDS test environments to train and ensure familiarity with the system’s general functionality, screen layout and navigation, and connectivity and transaction flows.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-md-4">
<div class="phases-card">
<span>6</span>
<h3>Go Live - Promotion to Production</h3>
<p>Schedule a Go-live date to transition your setup to full integration with CDSX Production. Begin real-time operations with the ongoing support of a dedicated Relationship Manager. </p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="new-banner" id="new">
<div class="container">
<div class="row">
